# Pass "sans-biotech": Core and the other DLCs, with Biotech left out of ModsConfig.
#
# The only DLC this mod touches is Biotech: the stove lists two baby-food recipes under MayRequire, and
# they have to drop out cleanly, with no unresolved recipe, when Biotech is not active. Leaving the other
# DLCs in is deliberate: they play no part in that guard, and the manual pass in ../../TESTING.md that runs
# Core alone still covers the case where all of them are absent.
#
# No save is played in this pass. The test-colony fixture was written with every DLC active, and its own
# errors about missing Biotech content would be read as this mod's. See @save in the features.
!ludeon.rimworld.biotech
